236,73.5,1952,60,107,22],[34237,62.3,1952,61,111,25],[34238,45.2,1952,62,111,23]],"links":[["Skagit County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/washington/skagit-county"],["ARC or PLC in Skagit County","/arc-plc/washington/skagit-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 16 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025, June to July came in at 33% of normal on the middle, and May to June at 53%. Every grid had its driest year in 1952, with grid 33934 down at 58% that year.</p>"}
